  "name": "Pirate Captain",
  "type": "adversary",
  "img": "icons/svg/skull.svg",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p><em>A charismatic sea dog, eager to raid and plunder.</em></p>\n",
    "attribution": {
      "source": "Heart & Dagger Manuscript"
    },
    "classification": "normal",
    "type": "leader",
    "difficulty": 14,
    "notes": "<h3>Normal | Leader</h3>\n<p><em>A charismatic sea dog, eager to raid and plunder.</em><br><strong>Motives &amp; Tactics:</strong> Command, plunder, raid</p>\n<p><strong>Difficulty:</strong> 14 | <strong>Thresholds:</strong> 7/14 | <strong>HP:</strong> 7 | <strong>Stress:</strong> 5</p>\n<p><strong>ATK:</strong> +4 | Weapon: Melee | 1d12+2 phy</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Experience:</strong> Commander +2, Sailor +3</p>\n<h4>Features</h4>\n<p><strong>Swashbuckler - Passive</strong>: When the Captain marks 2 or fewer HP from an attack in Melee, the attacker must <strong>mark a Stress</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Reinforcements - Action</strong>: Once per scene, <strong>mark a Stress</strong> to summon Pirate Raiders at Far range.</p>\n<p><strong>No Quarter - Action</strong>: Spend a Fear to target a foe with three or more Pirates in Melee. The Captain leads a chorus of threats; the target makes a Charm Reaction Roll. On a failure, they mark 1d4+1 Stress. On a success, they still mark 1 Stress.</p>\n<p><strong>Momentum - Reaction</strong>: When the Captain hits a PC with an attack, you gain a Fear.</p>\n",
    "damageThresholds": {
